  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 364 tests pass (30 new CSV export tests + 17 late fee + 20 VAT summary + 24 overdue + 273 existing).\n\n**`src/export.js` \u2014 New export module:**\n- `exportCsv(invoices)` \u2014 Exports invoices as standard CSV format\n\n**Output format:**\n- Header line: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n- One line per invoice in order given\n- All amounts formatted as plain euros: `1234.50` (2 decimals, dot separator, no currency sign)\n- No thousands separator in numbers\n- Lines end with `\\n`\n\n**CSV escaping rules:**\n- Double quotes around fields containing comma or quote\n- Double any internal quotes: `\"` becomes `\"\"`\n- Example: `Marlow \"The Print Shop\"` becomes `\"Marlow \"\"The Print Shop\"\"\"`\n\n**Field values:**\n- `number`: Invoice number (empty for draft)\n- `customer`: Customer name (from getCustomer lookup)\n- `issueDate`, `dueDate`, `status`: Direct from invoice\n- `subtotal`, `discount`, `vat`, `total`, `due`: Calculated and formatted as euros\n\n**Test coverage (30 new tests):**\n- Empty array, single invoice, multiple invoices\n- All field presence and correctness\n- Euro formatting (2 decimals, dot, no currency sign, no separators)\n- CSV escaping for commas and quotes\n- Draft, issued, partially_paid, paid invoices\n- Due amounts (zero for paid, balance for partial)\n- Large datasets (100+ invoices)\n- Immutability verification\n- Amount calculations verification\n- Order preservation\n- Edge cases with special characters in customer names\n\nFeature complete and ready to ship.",
